Running #VSLAM on #EyeTracking Glasses: the #PupilInvisible

🎬 Video: https://youtu.be/sXGqEjbZegM
🔗 VSLAM-LAB: https://lnkd.in/gGZifSb3
🔗 AllFeature-VSLAM: https://lnkd.in/gRztKMHT

I recorded a sequence walking around the living room wearing Pupil Invisible glasses from Pupil Labs: eye-tracking glasses with a forward-facing scene camera, worn like ordinary glasses. Egocentric footage is different from a hand-held or car-mounted camera: every glance is a rotation, every step a bounce, and the scene is an ordinary living room, textureless walls, close-range parallax, furniture everywhere.
🌐 Pupil Invisible: https://pupil-labs.com

I ran AllFeature-VSLAM in monocular mode, tightly coupling two feature types in the same map: ORB and ALIKED.Handcrafted and learned features, matched and optimised together in the same monocular pipeline.

A Pupil wrapper is available in VSLAM-LAB to record your own sequence with a Pupil AR device, point VSLAM-LAB at it, and it comes out in the VSLAM-LAB format, ready for every system in the benchmark. Try it on your own recordings.

Thanks to Tobias Fischer for lending me the Pupil Invisible glasses. Looking forward to running more experiments with these amazing devices — or with the Aria ones if I can get a pair :)

